3f0be674752b6728","file":"preprints/The-second-Kahn-Kalai-conjecture-September-24-2026/build/source/sections/introduction.tex","line":32,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"48a0beb109201b45c2adbf89a2f2e952cdcbef7419cb15078620ab42b4dedbc7","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-second-Kahn-Kalai-conjecture-September-24-2026/build/source/sections/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:5e02201b04fefc131ef9a8c2759070f01371d076043b0a273f0be674752b6728","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-second-Kahn-Kalai-conjecture-September-24-2026/build/source/sections/introduction.tex#L32"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nFor every $n\\ge2$ and every finite simple graph $H$ with $h=e(H)\\ge1$\nedges and at most $n$ vertices,\n\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:stronger}\n \\pc(n,H)\\le\n \\min\\{1,\\;2048\\ee^{50}\\pE(n,H)(1+\\log_2 h)\\}.\n\\end{equation}\nIn particular,\n\\[\n \\pc(n,H)\\le6144\\ee^{50}\\pE(n,H)\\log_2 n.\n\\]"}
